codex
The paper’s decisive facts are now clear: Theorems 1–3 turn “januarial” into an exact order/orbit test, while Theorem 5 and its corollary replace a full \(q+1\)-point coset-diagram traversal with a fixed-point/Euler-characteristic calculation. That creates a plausible Track B gap, but not Track A hardness. I’m checking whether that gap survives the repository’s guess-resistance, canonicalization, and no-tool caps before committing to a build.
