The more faithful family is not “construct a diagram and return its huge orbits.” The paper’s Lemma 1 canonically labels each januarial conjugacy class by an inverse pair \(\{z^i,z^{-i}\}\) inside a prime-order cyclic subgroup. I’m testing the inverse problem—recover that exponent pair—as a native PGL(2,p) discrete-log witness. It is inverse-generated, verifies by exact matrix powering, keeps the answer two integers long, and avoids the paper’s explicit-classification shortcut.
