codex
Implemented a native Track B generator based on the paper’s projective trace-parameter construction and Theorems 1–3/Section 4 ([paper PDF](https://arxiv.org/pdf/1810.00203)).

- [Generator](/home/gson/gvrepo/results/1810.00203/gen_1810_00203.py:37)
- [Self-test report](/home/gson/gvrepo/results/1810.00203/selftest_report.json:1)
- [README](/home/gson/gvrepo/results/1810.00203/README.md:1)
- [Bare transcript](/home/gson/gvrepo/results/1810.00203/llm_loop_transcript.jsonl:1)
- [Structural-hint transcript](/home/gson/gvrepo/results/1810.00203/g9_hinted_transcript.jsonl:1)
- [Placebo transcript](/home/gson/gvrepo/results/1810.00203/g9_placebo_transcript.jsonl:1)

All local gates pass. Key measurements:

- Guessing: 0/200,000; exact probability \(5.92\times10^{-8}\)
- Four attacks: 0/8 each
- Reference scan: 19,984 operations on the audit instance; 71,872 maximum across G6
- Compact route: 108 operations
- Answer: 116 characters, 24 atoms

The only blocker is Step 4: OpenRouter returned HTTP 403 “Key limit exceeded” for every bare, structural, and placebo call. Each transcript therefore contains four errors and zero valid attempts. They are preserved honestly, but the result is not submission-ready until the OpenRouter limit is replenished and the three hardening runs succeed.
